# Trains conductor UX invariants

Hard product rules. Prefer these over older skill/docs text when they conflict. **Confirm with the maintainer** before changing any of these.

See also: [trains.mdc](./trains.mdc), [trains-simple-advanced-modes.mdc](./trains-simple-advanced-modes.mdc).

## Terminology

| Term | Means | Do not confuse with |
|------|--------|---------------------|
| **Rule** (UI) | Conductor selection mechanism for a day (`conductorMechanism`, `ConductorMechanismType`, day paint) | Week **template** |
| **Eligibility** (UI) | Members who can be drawn for a rule (`conductor_pool_entries`, minimums, score gates) | Code `PoolType` / API `pool` |
| **Week template** (UI) | Collection of rules applied over a stretch of time, currently a full week (`WeekTemplateType`, composite templates) | A single day's rule |
| **Day rule** / day paint | One day's conductor (+ VIP) rule from `DAY_PAINT_TEMPLATES` | Week template names that contain "week" |
| **Lock** | `lockedAt` — conductor boarded / train spawned | VIP assignment |

**UI copy rule:** use **Rule** / **Eligibility** / **Week template** in officer-facing strings. Do **not** rename TS types, DB columns, or API fields in Phase 1-style copy-only work.

Guided flow first row: **"This day's rule"** — never label it "Week template".

## Day paint vs week templates (exclusive)

Canonical lists: `DAY_PAINT_TEMPLATES` vs selectable week/composites in `paint-templates.shared.ts` + `week-template-registry.shared.ts`.

| Surface | Options |
|---------|---------|
| Month — **one** day selected | Day mechanisms only — **no** composites |
| Month — **multiple** days | Week templates (composites OK) |
| Week strip — **Week template** control | Week / composite templates |
| Week strip — long-press / change day | Day mechanisms for that date only |
| Guided **"Change pick"** | **This day** via `DayMechanismPickerDialog` — never `WeekTemplatePickerDialog` |

- Do **not** put composites (e.g. `vs_push_week`) in single-day pickers.
- **Composite segment resolution** uses **calendar DOW relative to Tuesday** (Tue=0 … Mon=6) via `compositeSegmentDayIndex` in `src/lib/trains/week-template-registry.shared.ts` — **not** alliance `trainWeekStartDow`. A Monday-start train week must still paint Tue–Sat push and Sun–Mon R4 segments on the correct calendar days.
- Day-painted mechanism **sticks** unless impossible for that server date (e.g. TPIF on Monday bounces; Saturday **day** TPIF must not auto-rewrite to the week’s heavy-hitter segment).
- Changing a day’s conductor mechanism **releases** any unlocked pending conductor/VIP draft so the officer can spin again under the new mechanism.
- Composite Saturday segment **`takedown_week`** is **with-replacement** Price Is Freight heavy-hitter (`usesPriceIsFreightConductorRoll` in `src/lib/trains/heavy-hitter-pool.shared.ts`) — same path as legacy whole-week `price_is_right` Saturday, **not** a depleting pool.

## Lifecycle: conductor → lock → VIP

In-game: conductor boards (lock/spawn) **before** VIP can board.

- Guided order: `… → conductor → lock → vip → done` (`guided-flow.shared.ts` / `currentGuidedStep`).
- VIP assign/spin requires `lockedAt`. Server: `assignVipOnLockedConductor`; client gates: `canSpinVipForDay` / manual VIP only when locked.
- Do **not** put VIP before lock in UI, skill, or docs.

## Dates (server calendar)

- “Today” / eligibility uses **game server calendar** (`game-time`, UTC−2), not the browser local date.
- **Monday:** no prior-day **daily** VS for any conductor mechanism (T−1 Sunday is the VS break). Top VS / prior-day maps **short-circuit empty** — do not query Ashed for Sunday week-ending totals.
- **Sunday** draws that need prior-day VS use **Saturday** (Enemy Buster Day).
- Prior-day VS for wheels and PIF uses **daily** Ashed `VSScore` rows only. Exclude **`is_weekly` / `isWeekly`** week-ending totals (uploaded on Sunday `recorded_date`); they must never feed Monday trains or daily Top VS / ticket math.
- **Manual picks** (e.g. `r3_recognition`) are never blocked on missing/low VS scores.
- `r3_recognition` is **manual award only** — no R3 pool wheel.

## Pool rank, Top VS roster, conductor minimums

- **Pool rank eligibility** (`resolveMemberPoolAllianceRank`): when an HQ **`member_alliance_rank_events`** row exists, use that rank — **do not** `Math.max` with a stale **higher** synced Ashed roster rank after an in-game demotion. Fall back to synced roster / Ashed rank raw only when there is no HQ event yet.
- **Top VS** (`fetchAllianceVsTopScorersForTrainDate` / `fetchVsTopScorersForRecordedDate`):
  - **Dedupe** Ashed `VSScore` rows by member — keep the **max** score per `member_id` before sorting/slicing Top N (re-uploads must not inflate odds or push the true Nth scorer off the board).
  - **Intersect** with the **active HQ roster** (`listActiveAllianceMembersForPool`, exclude `former`) — same spirit as Top VR; departed members must not win the wheel.
- **Conductor minimums** (alliance VS / donation thresholds on `r3` / `heavy_hitter` pools): evaluate **Ashed daily VS** over the configured window (not season VR). Post-roll DQ and pool seed filtering apply when minimums are enabled — do not block the check on `classifyVsDataNeed` / guided `prerequisites`; missing VS data counts as zero for that period.

## Swap / make-up day

- Source: unlocked draft with a conductor (`canStartConductorSwap`).
- Targets: **strictly after** server today; never past or same day.
- Quick picks: next **3** unlocked future days (`conductorSwapCandidates`) — **may cross week boundaries**.
- Offer a date picker for farther future dates.
- Do **not** hide Swap on the last day of the current week.
- Both days must be unlocked (`swapConductors`).
- Swap **only moves drafts** — do **not** auto-lock. Lock when the train is set in-game.
- After swap, **re-stamp depleting-pool selection** for each day’s conductor (`selectedForDate` follows the new date). Unlock must **not** return a rolled member to the lottery — only clear/re-roll does.

## Spin for the week

- Rolls remaining wheel-eligible days and leaves them as **unlocked drafts**.
- Do **not** batch-lock from this flow — lock is the irreversible in-game spawn action.

## Week strip

- Every day tile always shows the conductor name or **"—"** (not only when selected).
- Long-press day paint uses `DAY_PAINT_TEMPLATES`.

## Share image / wheel readability

- Share → generate PNG → **preview** → **Copy Media** / **Download** / Close. Never auto-download on Share click.
- Re-export from guided Conductor step and advanced Today’s Conductor when a conductor exists (pending or locked).
- Frame: winner + surrounding pool names + confetti; eligibility stats when the draw required a score threshold; locale-format large numbers.
- **Conductor wheel UI** (`ConductorWheelModal`): use theme tokens (`text-hq-accent`, `text-hq-fg-muted`, dual-mode score colors) so names and VS scores stay readable in **light** theme — do not hardcode white-on-dark-only reel text.

## Wizard recovery (stay on `/trains`)

- Roster/pool blockers: in-flow Ashed sync when alliance + session allow; **Members** CTA only as last resort.
- Sync/upload dialogs: loading → success/error → next-step CTAs; refresh guided step state after success.
- `WheelBlockedDialog` CTAs must match the real blocker (upload prior-day VS vs sync roster vs reseed) — not a generic Members link when scores or Ashed sync would unblock.
- **Never offer reseed / “start new rotation” for `POOL_UNAVAILABLE`** — members remain in the current generation but none qualify (minimums, etc.). Offer manual pick instead. Reseed only for `POOL_EMPTY` or `POOL_EXHAUSTED`.
- Pool details **“Start new rotation”** is a new generation; confirm copy must warn when unpicked members remain. Show **prior generation** summaries when `generation > 1`.
- Disqualified-winner UI only when that mechanism actually required VS. If the wizard skipped scores (e.g. R4), do not show VS disqualification for a 0-score roster.

## Before implementing UX changes

1. Read this rule, `trains-simple-advanced-modes.mdc`, and `guided-flow.shared.ts` / swap / paint-template tests.
2. If changing step order, date eligibility, day/week paint lists, or share/swap flows — **confirm with the maintainer first**.
3. Update this rule in the same PR when product intent changes.
